          %p
            The notion of
            %em cograph of a functor
            is dual to that of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph+of+a+functor"} graph of a functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : C \to D
            a functor between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-categories"} n-categories
            is the fibration classified by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profunctor"} profunctor
            correspondence
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi χ
                      %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ×
                    %mi D
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_f : C^{op}\times D \to (n-1)Cat
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            also determines a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %mo :
                  %mi I
                  %mo →
                  %mi n
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar f : I \to n Cat
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval+category"} interval category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            %strong cograph
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is the fibration classified by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar f
          %p
            Recall that the graph of a function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: A \to B
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
            determined by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle 1, f \rangle: A \to A \times B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: A \to B
            is the categorically dual notion: it is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+object"} quotient
            determined by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊔
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f, 1): A \sqcup B \to B
          %p
            A more vivid presentation of cograph is given by the pictures we draw of functions
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: A \to B
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+graph"} directed graph
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊔
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \sqcup B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(a)
            for each
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi P
                    %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_f
            with underlying set
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊔
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \sqcup B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \leq f(a)
            and all other instances of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \leq
            are the reflexive ones. The connected components function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi P
                    %mi f
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 0
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi P
                    %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (P_f)_0 \to \pi_0(P_f)
            is then the cograph in the sense given above.
          %p
            In this article we give a definition of cograph which generalizes this poset picture of cograph of a function, and which applies to any functor between
            = succeed "-categories." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %h1#examples Examples
          %h2#cographs_of_functors_between_0categories Cographs of functors between 0-categories
          %p
            In the case that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C, D
            are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/0-category"} 0-categories
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : C \to D
            is just a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            between sets. The cograph
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-pullback"} 2-pullback
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi cograph
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi I
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mover
                              %mi f
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                        %mtd
                          %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  cograph(f) &amp;\to&amp; {*}
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  I &amp;\stackrel{\bar f}{\to}&amp; Set
                  }
          %p
            is computed by the ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi cograph
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi Set
                            %mo *
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi I
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mover
                              %mi f
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                        %mtd
                          %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  cograph(f) &amp;\to&amp; Set_{*}
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  I &amp;\stackrel{\bar f}{\to}&amp; Set
                  }
          %p
            and identifies
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi cograph
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cograph(f)
            with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+elements"} category of elements
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar f
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi cograph
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cograph(f)
            are the disjoint union of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Obj
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi cograph
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Obj(cograph(f)) = C \coprod D
            and the nontrivial morphisms are of the form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo →
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \to y
            whenever
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \in D
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x) = y
          %p
            What
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bill+Lawvere"} Bill Lawvere
            called the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cograph+of+a+function"} cograph of a function
            is the connected components
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Cograph
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0(Cograph(f))
            of this category.
          %h2#cographs_of_functors_between_1categories Cographs of functors between 1-categories
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : C \to D
            an ordinary
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi cograph
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cograph(f)
            is the category with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Obj
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi cograph
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi Obj
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                  %mi Obj
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Obj(cograph(f)) = Obj(C) \coprod Obj(D)
            and with
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mrow
                      %mi cograph
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mi C
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo ,
                            %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi if
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi x
                            %mo ,
                            %mi y
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi C
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mi D
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo ,
                            %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi if
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi x
                            %mo ,
                            %mi y
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi D
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mi D
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi if
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi x
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi C
                            %mo ,
                            %mi y
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi D
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ∅
                          %mtd
                            %mi if
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi x
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi D
                            %mo ,
                            %mi y
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Hom_{cograph(f)}(x,y) =
                  \\left\{
                  \\array{
                  Hom_C(x,y) &amp; if\; x,y \in C
                  \\\
                  Hom_D(x,y) &amp; if\; x,y \in D
                  \\\
                  Hom_D(f(x),y) &amp; if\; x \in C ,y \in D
                  \\\
                  \\emptyset &amp; if\; x \in D ,y \in C
                  }
                  \\right.
          %p
            with composition defined as induced from
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cograph+of+a+profunctor"} cograph of a profunctor
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profunctor"} profunctor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(f-,-)
          %p
            This cograph is denoted
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %msup
                    %mo ⋆
                    %mi f
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \star^f D
            in section 2.3.1 (_Correspondences_) in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} Higher Topos Theory
          %p
            where it is understood as a generalization of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/join+of+simplicial+sets"} join of simplicial sets
            and where it serves as a motivation for the study of cographs of functors between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-categories
            discussed below.
          %h2#AdjointFunctorsInTermsOfCographs Adjoint functors in terms of cographs
          %p
            As emphasized in the beginning of section 5.2 there, cographs of functors may be used to characterize
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjoint functors
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profunctors"} profunctors
            (which in turn makes sense in any
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category+equipped+with+proarrows"} 2-category equipped with proarrows
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Two functors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L : C \to D
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo :
                    %mi D
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R : D \to C
              are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjoint functors
              precisely if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi cograph
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cograph(L)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi cograph
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mi op
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cograph(R^{op})^{op}
              are isomorphic under
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              and
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⇔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi cograph
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi cograph
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mi op
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (L \dashv R) \Leftrightarrow
                    (cograph(L) \cong cograph(R^{op})^{op})
            %p
              where the isomorphism is in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/co-slice+category"} co-slice category
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo ⊔
                      %mi D
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi Cat
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C\sqcup D)/Cat
          %p
            More precisely, there is a bijection between adjunctions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L\dashv R
            and isomorphisms as above.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              The category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi cograph
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cograph(L)
              is the category with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Obj
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi cograph
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi Obj
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mi Obj
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Obj(cograph(L)) = Obj(C) \coprod Obj(D)
              and with
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %mi cograph
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi L
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi Hom
                                %mi C
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi x
                              %mo ,
                              %mi y
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mi if
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mi x
                              %mo ,
                              %mi y
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi C
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi Hom
                                %mi D
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi x
                              %mo ,
                              %mi y
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mi if
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mi x
                              %mo ,
                              %mi y
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi D
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi Hom
                                %mi D
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi L
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi x
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo ,
                              %mi y
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mi if
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mi x
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi C
                              %mo ,
                              %mi y
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi D
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi ∅
                            %mtd
                              %mi if
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mi x
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi D
                              %mo ,
                              %mi y
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Hom_{cograph(L)}(x,y) =
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    Hom_C(x,y) &amp; if\; x,y \in C
                    \\\
                    Hom_D(x,y) &amp; if\; x,y \in D
                    \\\
                    Hom_D(L(x),y) &amp; if\; x \in C ,y \in D
                    \\\
                    \\emptyset &amp; if\; x \in D ,y \in C
                    }
                    \\right.
            %p
              (This set is also called the set of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heteromorphisms"} heteromorphisms
              between objects in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              and
              = succeed ".)" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %p
              The category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi cograph
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mi op
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cograph(R^{op})^{op}
              accordingly is the category with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Obj
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi cograph
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi Obj
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mi Obj
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Obj(cograph(R)) = Obj(C) \coprod Obj(D)
              and with
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %mi cograph
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi R
                          %mi op
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi op
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi Hom
                                %mi C
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi x
                              %mo ,
                              %mi y
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mi if
                              %mi x
                              %mo ,
                              %mi y
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi C
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi Hom
                                %mi D
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi x
                              %mo ,
                              %mi y
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mi if
                              %mi x
                              %mo ,
                              %mi y
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi D
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi Hom
                                %mi C
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi x
                              %mo ,
                              %mi R
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi y
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mi if
                              %mi x
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi C
                              %mo ,
                              %mi y
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi D
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi ∅
                            %mtd
                              %mi if
                              %mi x
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi D
                              %mo ,
                              %mi y
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Hom_{cograph(R^{op})^{op}}(x,y) =
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    Hom_C(x,y) &amp; if x,y \in C
                    \\\
                    Hom_D(x,y) &amp; if x,y \in D
                    \\\
                    Hom_C(x,R(y)) &amp; if x \in C ,y \in D
                    \\\
                    \\emptyset &amp; if x \in D ,y \in C
                    }
                    \\right.
            %p
              Evidently these categories are isomorphic under
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              precisely if for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in C, y \in D
              we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≅
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Hom_D(L(x),y) \cong Hom_C(x,R(y))
                    \\,.
            %p
              naturally in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_D(L(-),-)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_C(-,R(-))
              is encoded by composition in the cograph. Of course, such a natural isomorphism is precisely the structure of an adjunction
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                      %mo ⊣
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L\dashv R
          %p
            Note also that just as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi cograph
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cograph(L)
            is the cograph of the profunctor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(L-,-)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi cograph
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi R
                    %mi op
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cograph(R^{op})^{op}
            is the cograph of the profunctor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi R
                    %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(-,R-)
            %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/2-category+equipped+with+proarrows#HomsetAdjn"} formulated
            in terms of profunctors in any 2-category equipped with proarrows.
          %h2#cographs_of_functors_between_categories
            Cographs of functors between
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            In the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            theory there is a good theory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+fibrations"} Cartesian fibrations
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to S
            and of their classification by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functors"} (∞,1)-functors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{op} \to (\infty,1)Cat
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-categories
            as described at
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+fibration+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} universal fibration of (∞,1)-categories
          %p
            Accordingly, the above notion of cograph of a functor has a direct generalization to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functors"} (∞,1)-functors
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : C \to D
              an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mo :
                    %mi I
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\bar f : I \to (\infty,1)Cat
            %p
              in the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-categories
              %strong cograph
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+fibration"} Cartesian fibration
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi cograph
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cograph(f) \to I
              classified by it. In terms of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+fibration+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} universal fibration of (∞,1)-categories
              this is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi cograph
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mi op
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi I
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mover
                                %mi f
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn ∞
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi Cat
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    cograph(f) &amp;\to&amp; S^{op}
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    I &amp;\stackrel{\bar f}{\to}&amp; (\infty,1)Cat
                    }
                    \\,.
          %p
            As for every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+fibration"} Cartesian fibration
            the functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : C \to D
            is determined uniquely up to equivalence by its cograph. In general, obtaining the classifying
            = succeed "-functor" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+fibration"} Cartesian fibration
            may be difficult. In the special case of cographs as Cartesian fibrations over the simple
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval+category"} interval category
            it is easier. This is discussed in the following:
          %p …
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph+of+a+functor"} graph of a functor
            %li
              %p
                %strong> cograph of a functor
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cograph+of+a+profunctor"} cograph of a profunctor
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The notion of cographs of
            = succeed "-functors" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "-functors" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "," do
              %em Correspondences and associated functors
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} Higher Topos Theory
              \.
